            <ArticleTitle>Recurrent pain syndromes in children: a streamlined approach.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>47-50, 52, 58 passim</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Healthy-appearing children with recurring aches or pains are a frustrating part of pediatric practice. The authors share their 20-year experience in a diagnostic dilemmas clinic, helpful hints from the literature, and a simplified approach that uses checklists to streamline diagnosis and treat children with nonorganic syndromes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
